  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145958",
      "title": "Sending Requests To API Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 321,
      "videoOrder": 298,
      "sourceHash": "9156dab4f7f0a84a5044b6261a018e7a75d5be0c51fb9d5168deb8258b76ea46",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.03,
          "end": 3.85,
          "en": "So, let's now connect everything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.85,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "And for this, in the front-end index.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 10.02,
          "en": "I now really want to send a HTTP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.02,
          "end": 12.53,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.53,
          "end": 16.1,
          "en": "So for this, here, I will use that fetch function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.1,
          "end": 20.9,
          "en": "And now we need the URL to which the request should be sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.9,
          "end": 24.32,
          "en": "Now, since we will target this API route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.32,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "the URL will be our current domain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 31.83,
          "en": "and then just /API/feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.83,
          "end": 35.08,
          "en": "We don't need to encode our current domain here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.08,
          "end": 37.49,
          "en": "because if we start with a slash here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.49,
          "end": 39.62,
          "en": "this will automatically be appended",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.62,
          "end": 43.51,
          "en": "as a absolute path right after our domain.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.51,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "So, it will be sent to the same domain automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 50.96,
          "en": "And then, there to the path /API/feedback targeting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.96,
          "end": 52.593,
          "en": "that feedback file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.51,
          "end": 55.66,
          "en": "Now, we want to configure this request though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.66,
          "end": 59.13,
          "en": "and set the method to POST.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.13,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "This is very important, so that we send",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.59,
          "en": "the post HTTP request because ,of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.59,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "we're looking for these kinds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 69.393,
          "en": "of requests here in our API route code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.98,
          "end": 73.3,
          "en": "Then, we also need to add our body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.3,
          "end": 76.83,
          "en": "So, the data that should be appended to the request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.83,
          "end": 80.06,
          "en": "And we do this with the body property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.06,
          "end": 82.56,
          "en": "Now, that data should be an object containing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 86.02,
          "en": "the entered email and feedback, and it should be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.02,
          "end": 88.94,
          "en": "with a email and a text property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.94,
          "end": 90.4,
          "en": "because that's what we're trying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.4,
          "end": 93.263,
          "en": "to access inside of our API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.69,
          "end": 97.82,
          "en": "So, here I'll then just create my request body object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.82,
          "end": 102.06,
          "en": "let's say, with a email property of enteredemail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.06,
          "end": 105.243,
          "en": "and a text property have enteredfeedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.15,
          "end": 108.24000000000001,
          "en": "And then, that's the body I want to set here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 112.12,
          "en": "but not as a standard JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.12,
          "end": 114.28999999999999,
          "en": "but instead converted to JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.28999999999999,
          "end": 117.363,
          "en": "with help of that JSON stringify method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 121.46,
          "en": "Now, we should also make it super clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.46,
          "end": 125.54,
          "en": "that we're sending JSON data by adding some special header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.54,
          "end": 129.08,
          "en": "with help of the headers property, which takes an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.08,
          "end": 132.26,
          "en": "where we add the content type header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.26,
          "end": 136.67000000000002,
          "en": "so a key of content type added to this header object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.67000000000002,
          "end": 139.573,
          "en": "which is set to application/json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.6,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "And my key name is wrapped between single quotes here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 147.42000000000002,
          "en": "because I have a special character in this property name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.42000000000002,
          "end": 150.1,
          "en": "which wouldn't be allowed otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.1,
          "end": 153.18,
          "en": "So, now we add this object to add metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.18,
          "end": 156.8,
          "en": "to this request, which we're sending, informing the backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.8,
          "end": 159.13,
          "en": "informing the API route in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.13,
          "end": 163.16,
          "en": "that this request will carry JSON data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.16,
          "end": 166.48,
          "en": "That is required for the API routes feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.48,
          "end": 170.17000000000002,
          "en": "for Next.js therefore to correctly parse",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.4,
          "en": "the incoming request body, and convert JSON to JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.4,
          "end": 177.56,
          "en": "for us so that we can conveniently access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 177.56,
          "end": 179.653,
          "en": "it as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.45,
          "end": 183.88,
          "en": "So, that's how we sent this request now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.88,
          "end": 187.15,
          "en": "And then, here we can also listen to the response",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 187.15,
          "end": 190.82,
          "en": "and extract the JSON data from that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.82,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "And then, work with that data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 197.07,
          "en": "and maybe just console lock the data for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.07,
          "end": 198.75,
          "en": "So, we're just sending the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 198.75,
          "end": 201.89,
          "en": "and then, for the response, we're just extracting the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.89,
          "end": 205.98,
          "en": "and then logging the data, using the then methods here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.98,
          "end": 208.193,
          "en": "because fetch returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 209.11,
          "end": 212.1,
          "en": "With all that done, if you save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 212.1,
          "end": 215.38,
          "en": "you should be able to go back to your page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.38,
          "end": 217.72,
          "en": "and then enter any data of your choice here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.48,
          "end": 221.333,
          "en": "and click Send Feedback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.23,
          "end": 224.72,
          "en": "And, now, to find out whether this worked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 224.72,
          "end": 227.11,
          "en": "we can go to the feedback.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 227.11,
          "end": 229.76,
          "en": "And, in there, you should now have an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 229.76,
          "end": 234.76,
          "en": "which does contain one object with a ID property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.9,
          "end": 238.03,
          "en": "which is set to some automatically created ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.03,
          "end": 241.53,
          "en": "email, and text with values being equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 241.53,
          "end": 244.98,
          "en": "to the values you just entered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.98,
          "end": 247.83,
          "en": "So, that was now updated automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.83,
          "end": 250.433,
          "en": "because of our API route code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 251.84,
          "end": 254.86,
          "en": "And if I send another feedback,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.86,
          "end": 259.68,
          "en": "like does this work again from test2@test.com,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 259.68,
          "end": 261.92,
          "en": "if I click Send Feedback and we have a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.92,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "at feedback.json again, we see now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 267.58,
          "en": "that this was stored in there as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.58,
          "end": 270.72,
          "en": "And it's this array, which is being updated over time here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.72,
          "end": 274.72,
          "en": "which gets longer and longer with more and more elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.72,
          "end": 277.38,
          "en": "And this is all JSON data in there which is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.38,
          "end": 280.64,
          "en": "why the property names are wrapped by double quotes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.64,
          "end": 284.07,
          "en": "It looks like JavaScript, like a JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.07,
          "end": 286.96,
          "en": "and that's the entire idea behind JSON,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.96,
          "end": 289.77,
          "en": "it's this JavaScript object notation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.77,
          "end": 291.86,
          "en": "but it isn't a JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.86,
          "end": 293.48,
          "en": "It indeed just looks like it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 293.48,
          "end": 296.53,
          "en": "It is JSON formatted data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.53,
          "end": 300.35,
          "en": "because that's what we're doing in the feedback API route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 300.35,
          "end": 303.88,
          "en": "And now, with that, we achieved something important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 303.88,
          "end": 307.41,
          "en": "Now, in our next application, we are also able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.41,
          "end": 309.95,
          "en": "to work with submitted data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.95,
          "end": 314.95,
          "en": "we're not limited to just returning pages for get requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 315.56,
          "end": 317.74,
          "en": "And that allows us to add features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 317.74,
          "end": 321.37,
          "en": "like newsletter signup, feedback submission, comments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 321.37,
          "end": 325.52,
          "en": "or any other kind of data that should be submitted maybe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 325.52,
          "end": 328.1,
          "en": "And you don't have to build a separate API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 328.1,
          "end": 331.3,
          "en": "as a separate project, instead, you can easily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.3,
          "end": 334.40999999999997,
          "en": "add API routes your website might need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 334.40999999999997,
          "end": 337.43,
          "en": "as part of your Next.js project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 337.43,
          "end": 341.653,
          "en": "That's why API routes are a great and very useful feature.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
